":"https://github.com/norepro","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T06:15:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T06:15:42Z","body":"> There are two severe problems here:\r\n> \r\n>     * The single-view mode having a background breaks visual consistency with the rest of the docks.\r\n> \r\n>     * The horizontal split-view mode backgrounds have no margins, so they just hug the borders.\r\n\r\nFair. This issue is more complicated than I thought... my goal was to make it self-consistent among split modes. But I am guessing way more users see the default single-view than split and,by comparison, it is the odd one out.\r\n\r\nI also see the second point. I was focused more on the colors and usability and missed that detail.\r\n\r\nI'll mark this PR as draft while I consider options here and bring up any ideas in the discussion thread.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4448146120/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4467016035","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119450#issuecomment-4467016035","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/r